  "ideographicDescription": "⿰彳⿱幺夂[GJKV]",
  "confidence": 93,
  "verificationStatus": "cross-verified",
  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "One step 彳 coming behind another 夂; 幺 provides the pronunciation"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Phonosemantic compound. 幺 represents the sound, and 彳 (walk) and 夂 (foot) are used together to depict following behind someone."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "遲也。从彳、幺、夊者，後也。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "In oracle bone script, ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 幺 (“thread”) + 夊 (“foot”) – a foot bound by a rope, thus lagging behind. The component 彳 was added afterwards to emphasize this action.\nNote that the simplified form 后 is also a traditional character on its own, with a different meaning.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *hwak (“below”) (STEDT). Cognate with Tibetan འོག ('og, “below”), Burmese အောက် (auk, “under; below”) (from Proto-Lolo-Burmese *ʔok (“lower side; below”))."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "遲也。从彳、幺、夊者，後也。",
